The recurrent-state leak experiment (lesson 9535ad01), against llama.cpp
035e227. Apply from the source root with `patch -p1`, build as
serve/crates/sovereign-compute/llama-server/build.sh --vanilla does, run with LLAMA_LEAK_CLEAR set.

LLAMA_LEAK_CLEAR=1     llama_memory_clear(data = true) whenever a slot starts
                       from position 0: drift 0.0 nats (probes.py leak), A/A
                       0 of 47 greedy cases unstable (battery-20261011-111305)
LLAMA_LEAK_CLEAR=meta  the same with data = false: drift unchanged, so the
                       leak is stale state data, not cell bookkeeping
LLAMA_LEAK_HALF=recr   zero only the recurrent half's data: drift 0.0035 nats
LLAMA_LEAK_HALF=attn   zero only the attention half's: drift unchanged, and
                       the first probe moves (-1.155 against -1.0795), a
                       deterministic anomaly not yet explained

An experiment, not a fix: llama_memory_clear wipes every sequence, so it is
only sound when no other slot holds state worth keeping.

